 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "bosch 24 not draining, water sitting in bottom. help"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "I can help with that. Standing water in a Bosch dishwasher usually means it hasn't been able to pump out, most often because something is blocking the filter or sump area, or the drain hose is kinked. Please start by taking out the lower rack and twisting out the main cylindrical filter at the bottom of the tub. Rinse it under the tap and look into the sump (the hole underneath) with a torch for any debris like glass, stones, or food. Also check if the small impeller fan blade inside is free to turn by hand. Did you find anything blocked there, and does the impeller spin freely?\n[Helpful to see: image \"Where the filter is\" — The filter sits in the base of the dishwasher, usually under the bottom spray arm. Twist it out anticlockwise and rinse it under a tap. Typical layout — your dishwasher may differ.]"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "filter was clogged with food and a bit of broken glass. impeller turns fine. cleaned it, drains ok now and E:24 gone"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That’s excellent news. To help prevent this from happening again, I’d suggest giving the filter a quick rinse under the tap every few washes, especially if you’re scraping plates rather than rinsing them thoroughly first. If it runs smoothly for a while longer, you can be confident the issue is fully resolved."
  }
 ],
